  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CERF contribution 2014</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The CERF, the UN Central Emergency Fund, was established in 2006 as part of the efforts to make the UN system better able to respond quickly in emergency humanitarian crises and to provide assistance to crises that are chronically under-funded. UN-OCHA, which coordinates the international relief, manages the fund, which is financed solely by voluntary contributions, which consists of two windows; a &quot;rapid response&quot; and one for &quot;underfunded emergencies&quot;. UN target the CERF to have at least 450 million USD available for emergencies every year, and preferably more. In 2014. Denmark supported the CERF with 150 million. DKK, out of which 50 mio. DKK constituted an extraordinary grant (beyond the 2014 National Finance Bill)</narrative>
  </description>
